---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME, SITE_DOMAIN } from '../lib/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'summary', label: 'The short version' },
  { id: 'using-the-service', label: 'Using the service' },
  { id: 'your-content', label: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'accuracy', label: 'Accuracy and results' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'our-work', label: 'Our work' },
  { id: 'availability', label: 'Availability and changes' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Disclaimers and liability' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to these terms' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title={`Terms & Conditions | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description={`The terms for using ${SITE_NAME}, a free resume builder and cover letter maker. Plain-language and short.`}
  eyebrow="Terms & conditions"
  heading="The rules, in plain language."
  lead="By using this site you agree to the terms below. We’ve kept them short and readable, because they should be."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p class="legal-note">
      The tool is free to use. What you write is yours. Please use it honestly, and understand it is
      provided as is, with no guarantee of a job.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms apply to {SITE_NAME} at {SITE_DOMAIN} (“we”, “us”, “the site”). If you do not
      agree with them, please do not use the site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="using-the-service">
    <h2>Using the service</h2>
    <p>
      You can use the resume builder, cover letter editor, templates, importer and exports for free,
      for personal or professional job applications, with no account required. You must be old enough
      to enter a binding agreement where you live, or have a parent or guardian’s permission.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-content">
    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep full ownership of everything you create, including your resume and cover letter text.
      Your content is processed and stored on your own device, and we do not claim any rights to it.
      You are responsible for what you write and for keeping a backup, since we cannot recover content
      stored in your browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="accuracy">
    <h2>Accuracy and results</h2>
    <p>
      We provide templates, layout and guidance, but you are responsible for the accuracy of your
      resume. Please only state experience, qualifications and dates that are true. We make no promise
      that a resume made here will pass any particular applicant tracking system, earn an interview or
      lead to a job. ATS ratings shown on templates are general guidance, not a guarantee.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sample content, role blueprints and example text are placeholders. Replace them with your own
      details and check them before you send anything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use">
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Please do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use the site to create false, misleading or fraudulent documents;</li>
      <li>attempt to disrupt, overload or break the site or its security;</li>
      <li>scrape or copy the site at scale, or resell the site or its templates as your own product;</li>
      <li>use the site in a way that breaks the law or infringes anyone’s rights.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="our-work">
    <h2>Our work</h2>
    <p>
      The site’s design, code, templates, text, logo and name belong to us or our licensors and are
      protected by copyright and other laws. You may use the documents you export for your own job
      search. You may not copy the site itself or its templates to build a competing product.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="availability">
    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep the site available, but it may be interrupted, changed or discontinued at any
      time, and features may be added or removed. Because your drafts are stored in your browser,
      please export a PDF of anything important.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or
      implied. To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect or
      consequential loss, loss of data, or loss of opportunity arising from your use of the site.
      Nothing in these terms limits any right or liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows when they last changed,
      and continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or use
      the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
